    "body": "Those seem good to me.\r\n\r\nFWIW: The anonymity of `optional` from my POV was that it’s a terminal symbol that’s not assigned a name, whereas the terminal symbol “decimal” say is expressly given a referenceable name. That the code point sequence described by the literal `optional` reads as a word in this case (but not in the case of e.g. `[`) didn’t seem to change this to me — but I’m just explaining my rationale, not arguing for it. I think that “regex” and “inline” are probably better choices and require much less explanation :)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
