    "created_at": "2022-10-11T22:03:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-11T22:03:13Z",
    "body": "> \"literal terminal symbol\"\r\n\r\nI agree that this is a good description. My only concern is that it may make it even easier to miss that these are “genuine” terminal symbols on the same footing as those defined using regular expressions, [not “refinements”](https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/issues/812) that constrain the latter to specific source character sequences as is common in [other language specs](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-terminal-symbols). Maybe that’s a separate issue, but it’s caused repeated problems, so I worry about confusing it further.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
